  "notes": [
    "Brew 1 tea bag in 8 oz (240 ml) of freshly boiled water (205°F–212°F / 96°C–100°C) for 3 to 5 minutes.",
    "Sourced from Yunnan Province, China, this blend pairs earthy, fermented pu'erh tea with sweet peppermint and botanical accents.",
    "Unlike standard black tea, which undergoes only oxidation, pu'erh is traditionally post-fermented, resulting in a dark, velvety brew with minimal bitterness and low astringency.",
    "Spacious full-leaf bags allow whole leaves and herbs sufficient room to unfurl and circulate, yielding a fuller flavor profile than conventional finely cut tea dust.",
    "The sturdy fermented leaves can often be re-steeped for a second cup by extending the infusion time slightly."
